# systemd account management is sysusers-native (no user/group/dir/file
# stanzas here by design): the package ships authoritative sysusers.d
# declarations with Saphira-pinned fixed IDs (meson -D for the
# templated confs, files/sysusers-static-ids.patch for the two static
# ones), and the generated post-install/post-upgrade runs
# systemd-sysusers after the reconciler. A second handwritten census
# would drift (it once missed imds and coredump entirely); instead the
# regression rule asserts every shipped identity-declaring conf is
# covered. ensure-identity remains for ordinary packages without a
# native account mechanism.
sysusers
